## 2025-11-07 ~16:00
**File**: infra/lib/agent-core-development.ts
**Changes**: Added full mesh IAM permissions for supervisor-to-supervisor invocations. Implemented nested loop that grants each supervisor agent permission to invoke all other supervisor agents using `grantInvokeRuntime()`. This creates a fully connected mesh topology where any supervisor can invoke any other supervisor, enabling hierarchical agent patterns where supervisors can delegate to or coordinate with peer supervisors. The logic uses an identity check (`if (supervisor !== otherSupervisor)`) to avoid granting self-invocation permissions. Also cleaned up whitespace formatting in the supervisor configuration loop for better code readability.

## 2025-11-07 ~16:05
**File**: src/agent001/main.py
**Changes**: Fixed Python lambda closure bug in MCP client initialization. Added default argument `url=mcp_url` to the lambda function to capture the loop variable value at definition time instead of reference time. Changed from `lambda: aws_iam_streamablehttp_client(endpoint=mcp_url, ...)` to `lambda url=mcp_url: aws_iam_streamablehttp_client(endpoint=url, ...)`. This prevents late binding issues where all lambda functions would reference the final value of `mcp_url` from the loop instead of their respective values. Critical fix to ensure each MCP client connects to the correct agent endpoint rather than all clients connecting to the last agent in the loop.


